    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d99">

                <pb facs="0105" n="95" xml:id="pg95"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Portugal/1434: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Norweb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-25T11:00:00+00:00">February 25,
                            1944—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 25—10:53 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>586. I assume that your 539 February 24, 11 a.m. implies that you are taking
                    steps to ensure (repeat ensure) that the British Ambassador will receive
                    instructions from London to join with me in requesting a temporary embargo on
                    wolfram exports. I shall, of course, not act alone pending his receipt of such
                    instructions.</p>
                <p>Repeated to London as 89. Sent Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Norweb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
